| **Ocean Acidification** (Long-term) | $\text{CO}_2$ absorption lowers ocean pH. | Corals struggle to build and maintain their skeletons. |
| **Pollution/Runoff** (Local) | Excess nutrients and sediment smother the coral. | Weakens the coral and promotes competing algae growth. |
| **Physical Damage** (Local) | Anchors, dredging, and fishing break the coral. | Creates wounds and stress points, increasing disease risk. |<turn|>
